## Description

In his last eleven months, Tupac recorded 150 songs, filmed three movies, dropped two albums and toured two continents. Most artists don't do that in a whole career. Read that again.

This one took us almost two years to make. We dug through old interviews, studio footage, stories from the people who were actually in those rooms, all chasing one question: how was one man moving that fast? Everybody talks about Tupac's speed. Nobody really explains it. 🎥

So we sat down and broke the whole thing apart. And what we found in the way this man operated... honestly, some of it will mess with how you see your own work. There's game in here for anybody building anything.

Because the numbers aren't even the story. What was driving them is. Tupac ran on something most people spend their whole lives trying to bury. He built a career on it. 🔥

If you think you grind, watch what this man did with eleven months.

